<div class="sql-sheet-shell">
    <section class="sql-sheet-hero">
        <div>
            <p class="sql-sheet-kicker">IB A3 Databases</p>
            <h1 class="sql-sheet-title">SQL Worksheets</h1>
            <p class="sql-sheet-summary">
                Work in sequence. The first worksheet is only about reading a schema and writing clean
                <code>SELECT</code> queries. The second moves on to sorting, pattern matching, joins, and a
                first grouped report. The third opens a blank workspace so students build the database
                themselves with <code>DDL</code> and <code>DML</code>. Higher Level students then continue
                with aggregate functions: <code>COUNT</code>, <code>AVG</code>, <code>SUM</code>,
                <code>MAX</code>, <code>MIN</code>, <code>GROUP BY</code>, and <code>HAVING</code>.
            </p>
            <div class="sql-chip-row">
                <span class="sql-chip"><i class="fa-solid fa-magnifying-glass"></i> Basic retrieval first</span>
                <span class="sql-chip"><i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-down-a-z"></i> Sorting and joins next</span>
                <span class="sql-chip"><i class="fa-solid fa-table-columns"></i> Build from scratch last</span>
                <span class="sql-chip"><i class="fa-solid fa-calculator"></i> HL aggregates</span>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="sql-sheet-actions">
            <a class="sql-launch" href="/tools/sql-playground.html?dataset=school-library" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
                <i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-up-right-from-square"></i>
                Open SQL Playground
            </a>
            <a class="sql-secondary-link" href="/ib-2027/A3/index.html">
                <i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-left"></i>
                Back to A3
            </a>
        </div>
    </section>

    <div class="sql-outline-grid">
        <section class="sql-outline-card">
            <h2>How to Use the Sequence</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>Keep the worksheet in one tab and the playground in another.</li>
                <li>Do not jump ahead: each dataset assumes the previous one is already secure.</li>
                <li>The final SL worksheet opens a blank workspace because students are building the schema themselves.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>
        <section class="sql-outline-card">
            <h2>SL Coverage</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>A3.1 relational features, keys, integrity, benefits, and limitations</li>
                <li>A3.2 schema reading, ERDs, data types, table structure, normal forms, and 3NF thinking</li>
                <li>A3.3 <code>SELECT</code>, filtering, ordering, joins, plus <code>CREATE</code>, <code>INSERT</code>, <code>UPDATE</code>, and <code>DELETE</code></li>
            </ul>
        </section>
    </div>

    <div class="sql-hub-grid">
        <article class="sql-hub-card">
            <p class="sql-sheet-kicker">Worksheet 1 | Core Retrieval</p>
            <h2>School Library</h2>
            <p>
                Start here. Use one clean three-table database to learn the structure of a relational model,
                then practise <code>SELECT</code>, <code>FROM</code>, <code>WHERE</code>, <code>AND</code>,
                and <code>OR</code> without extra SQL features getting in the way.
            </p>
            <div class="sql-chip-row">
                <span class="sql-chip">A3.1.1</span>
                <span class="sql-chip">A3.2.1</span>
                <span class="sql-chip">A3.3.2</span>
            </div>
            <div class="sql-link-row">
                <a class="sql-launch" href="/ib-2027/A3/sql-worksheets/school-library.html">Open worksheet</a>
                <a class="sql-secondary-link" href="/tools/sql-playground.html?dataset=school-library" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open dataset</a>
            </div>
        </article>

        <article class="sql-hub-card">
            <p class="sql-sheet-kicker">Worksheet 2 | Next-Step Queries</p>
            <h2>Campus Clubs</h2>
            <p>
                Move here once basic filtering is secure. This worksheet assumes students already know
                retrieval basics and focuses on <code>ORDER BY</code>, <code>DISTINCT</code>,
                <code>LIKE</code>, <code>BETWEEN</code>, joins, and a first
                <code>GROUP BY</code> report.
            </p>
            <div class="sql-chip-row">
                <span class="sql-chip">A3.2.2</span>
                <span class="sql-chip">A3.2.4</span>
                <span class="sql-chip">A3.3.2</span>
            </div>
            <div class="sql-link-row">
                <a class="sql-launch" href="/ib-2027/A3/sql-worksheets/campus-clubs.html">Open worksheet</a>
                <a class="sql-secondary-link" href="/tools/sql-playground.html?dataset=campus-clubs" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open dataset</a>
            </div>
        </article>

        <article class="sql-hub-card">
            <p class="sql-sheet-kicker">Worksheet 3 | Build the Database</p>
            <h2>Canteen Orders</h2>
            <p>
                Finish the SL sequence by building the database yourself in a blank workspace. Students work
                from the schema and ERD, create the tables, insert starter rows in batches, and then apply
                <code>UPDATE</code> and <code>DELETE</code>.
            </p>
            <div class="sql-chip-row">
                <span class="sql-chip">A3.2.4</span>
                <span class="sql-chip">A3.2.6</span>
                <span class="sql-chip">A3.3.1</span>
                <span class="sql-chip">A3.3.3</span>
            </div>
            <div class="sql-link-row">
                <a class="sql-launch" href="/ib-2027/A3/sql-worksheets/canteen-orders.html">Open worksheet</a>
                <a class="sql-secondary-link" href="/tools/sql-playground.html?dataset=__blank_workspace__" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open blank workspace</a>
            </div>
        </article>

        <article class="sql-hub-card">
            <p class="sql-sheet-kicker">Worksheet 4 | HL Focus</p>
            <h2>Course Enrolment Reporting</h2>
            <p>
                Use a ready-made HL dataset to practise grouped counts, averages, totals, highest and
                lowest values, and grouped filtering with <code>HAVING</code>.
            </p>
            <div class="sql-chip-row">
                <span class="sql-chip">COUNT</span>
                <span class="sql-chip">AVG</span>
                <span class="sql-chip">SUM</span>
                <span class="sql-chip">MAX / MIN</span>
                <span class="sql-chip">HAVING</span>
            </div>
            <div class="sql-link-row">
